# The crew: one astronaut per player, one line per ship, in ship order.
# Edit names here and re-run tools/lvc.py; no code changes needed.
#
#   crew <name> ship <ship name> [quirk <quirk from fleet.lv>] [tag <word>]... [flagship]
#        [habit "<one sentence about {A}>"]
#
# Tags are optional flavour hooks for cards: `when tag A mech` only binds role A to crew
# carrying that tag. Use them to let a card *prefer* someone (pair it with an untagged
# twin), never to lock a whole storyline to one person. Tags never appear in card text.
#
# With no quirk, the astronaut's starting traits are seeded from the voyage key and
# their name, so they are stable from build to build but nobody picked them.
# Card text never assumes anyone's gender: use {A}/{B} or "they".
#
# Habits: one small, harmless, real detail per astronaut, sent in by that player and
# dropped in here. It is a whole sentence about {A}, e.g.
#   habit "{A} keeps one small thing from home within reach of the console."
# Cards marked `each crew` print the first habit (one clone per astronaut, compiled in;
# the phone never sees a new slot). Up to four habits per line: `each habit N` cards
# clone only for astronauts with a real Nth habit, so a quirk line only ever renders
# for its owner. Never invent a habit for a real person: leave it out (or leave the
# placeholder), and no clone is made. To add a ship, add one line here; the
# engine's crew count (lv/state.N, tools/lvc.py N_CREW) must match.

crew Phill     ship Ship 01   tag controls  flagship  habit "{A} keeps a pot of galley herbs alive under a spare lamp, pinching it back like the beds at home." habit "{A} measures twice and drills once on a loose locker hinge, then adds \"hinges\" to the house to-do list waiting on Earth." habit "{A} plays the long cruise like a long grind: one daily list, small wins ticked off, no cutscenes skipped."
crew Jacques   ship Ship 02   tag controls  habit "{A}'s kit is squared away past any inspection: straps dressed, pens taped, every call answered \"copy\" first." habit "{A} checks a stock portfolio on prices fifteen minutes stale before they leave Earth. \"Long position,\" {A} says." habit "On entry eve {A} lays the suit out in donning order and runs the fleet's radio check in ninety crisp seconds."
crew Kim       ship Ship 03   tag controls  habit "{A} rations the episodes queued for the trip, one a week, and the fleet has learned not to call during one." habit "{A} names things. The water processor has a name and a backstory now, and the ground uses the name in tickets." habit "On the last corridor burn {A} allows the countdown one line of dramatic narration, then flies it dead straight."
crew Jai       ship Ship 04   tag controls  habit "{A} runs the hatch drill like a breach: stack up, check corners, clear the module, \"room clear\" before the list says it." habit "On the flyby plot {A} draws the trajectory as a racing line, apex marked. The nav team keeps the word." habit "{A} feels the last burn start a beat before the console shows it, like grip going in a sim, and the data agrees."
crew Michelle  ship Ship 05   tag controls  habit "Every data drop brings {A} a photo of the foster litter at home, counted for the record, one always out of frame." habit "{A} runs a crossing like a head count at feeding time: heads at the hatch, heads at the far side, no strays." habit "Last mail before entry: the litter {A} saw born has gone to homes, and the house is briefly, suspiciously quiet."
crew Diego     ship Ship 06   tag mech  habit "{A} cat-proofs the cabin out of habit: cables clipped, nothing on a ledge, latches double-thrown. No cats aboard." habit "Mail from whoever is minding {A}'s two cats: both fed, both offended, one asleep in the bag {A} meant to pack." habit "{A} redraws a sagging locker bracket on a ration wrapper, lighter and stiffer; the ground files it as a drawing."
crew Dorian    ship Ship 07   tag controls  habit "Every data drop brings {A} a drawing from a small boy at home: the ship, Mars and a dog, all the same size." habit "{A} asks the ship's assistant to summarise the fault log. It answers in one confident paragraph; {A} checks every line." habit "Last video before entry: a Boston terrier at the front window, and a small voice telling it {A} is nearly there."
crew Marco     ship Ship 08   tag controls  habit "{A} builds the galley playlist for the week and times the coffee to land on the drop." habit "{A} retunes the pump timer so its cycle lands on the beat. The ground asks, politely, why the log is in four-four." habit "Last mail before entry: {A}'s friends in a dark, loud room, holding up a sign: SAVING YOUR SPOT."
